ally what's what's happening here  and the question is do you lock down you  know  the decision was made to lock down nine  million people when in fact  uh there are these particular hot spot  areas  that are very alarming but that you know  there's a six-fold difference even in  london  between the rates of new infections so  it is complicated and i think people  need to find out what the  local data is in their area and if you  can stop people moving between  areas you know that should be doable so  i do think we need a  longer term approach to this that isn't  locking everything down  crippling the economy for areas that  have very low  uh levels of infection and i think you  know  that's the that's the big message here  this christmas in a way you do want  different rules for different areas  and i think um you know it may sound  unfair but that's the scientific uh  argument so on the basis of the data  you're gathering and then looking  forward  uh into january and february we  there are fears that i've referred to  that the christmas uh  easing up will lead to a spike or a  resurgence in cases  and then there is also a talk of a third  wave i think you have some views on that  yourself what does january february look  like to you  well i'm not as worried about seasonal  flu as james was  all the data show that we're at 10 of  the normal  uh rates of respiratory infections so it  just shows you that we can prevent  uh the normal colds and flus you know  i haven't had a cold all year it's fine  for a year it's fantastic  because we're not mixing we're not  mixing exactly  so we're not going to get a massive uh  influx of flu that was feared  and most people thought we would but  they haven't factored in our  amazing behavioral changes so i think  it's it's going to be  really all about uh covid uh  and if this will come in you know i  think we will get rid of this second  wave  um and i think there will be a lull and  we will see another one probably  uh in in f